An abort restores the modes of the move motion was on, from its state tag, but
not the spindle speed. The interpreter had already read ahead to G17 G97, so the
restore has a G96 with no S word. That failed the whole restore line with nothing
to show for it, leaving the plane and everything else as read ahead. This aborts
test.ngc during the G96 move and checks that the plane is back to G18, that the
spindle stays stopped and that no error is reported.
